    {
      "type": "grammar",
      "title": "<ico-book></ico-book> HAVE / HAS · posesivos",
      "intro": "Para decir lo que tienes usas <b>have</b>; con he / she / it cambia a <b>has</b>. Los posesivos (my, his, her…) dicen de quién es algo.",
      "parts": [
        {
          "type": "phrases",
          "items": [
            {
              "en": "I have two brothers.",
              "sp": "Tengo dos hermanos."
            },
            {
              "en": "She has a dog.",
              "sp": "Con he / she / it: <b>has</b>."
            },
            {
              "en": "Do you have a big family?",
              "sp": "Pregunta con do. Respuesta: Yes, I do. / No, I don't."
            },
            {
              "en": "His name is Tom. Her name is Ana.",
              "sp": "<b>his</b> = de él · <b>her</b> = de ella. En español los dos son «su»."
            },
            {
              "en": "My mother is a teacher.",
              "sp": "Las profesiones llevan <b>a / an</b>."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "cells",
          "cells": [
            {
              "h": "have / has",
              "body": "I/you/we/they <code>have</code><br>he/she/it <code>has</code><br><span class=\"es\">She <b>has</b> a dog. I <b>have</b> two brothers.</span>"
            },
            {
              "h": "negativo / pregunta",
              "body": "I <code>don't have</code> · she <code>doesn't have</code><br><code>Do</code> you have…? · <code>Does</code> he have…?"
            },
            {
              "h": "posesivos",
              "body": "I→<b>my</b> · you→<b>your</b> · he→<b>his</b><br>she→<b>her</b> · we→<b>our</b> · they→<b>their</b>"
            },
            {
              "h": "ejemplo",
              "body": "<span class=\"ok\">This is my sister.</span><br><span class=\"ok\">His name is Tom.</span> · <span class=\"ok\">Her job is nice.</span>"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "note",
          "gold": true,
          "body": "<b>Tres trampas del español:</b> <s class='x'>She is teacher.</s> → <span class='ok'>She is a teacher.</span> · <s class='x'>He has thirty years.</s> → <span class='ok'>He is thirty years old.</span> · «su nombre» puede ser <b>his</b> name o <b>her</b> name: mira de quién hablas."
        },
        {
          "type": "stretch",
          "h": "A2 · EXTRA",
          "body": "Posesivo con <b>'s</b>: \"Ana<b>'s</b> brother is a doctor.\" · Plurales: brother → brother<b>s</b>, child → child<b>ren</b>, person → people."
        }
      ],
      "stage": false
